From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Lopez <norelec@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:02:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Pack the Linux build as a Flatpak bundle

scripts/make-flatpak.sh packs bin/dist into a .flatpak on the freedesktop 25.08
runtime, with the .NET 10 runtime plugins need taken from the SDK extension.
The wrapper runs launcher and client in the app's data folder
(~/.var/app/io.github.Norelec91.WispUO/data), copies the bundled plugins there
on first run since an assistant writes into its own folder, and points
DOTNET_ROOT at the bundled runtime. Permissions: network, X11 for the launcher,
Wayland, PulseAudio, the GPU and the home folder read only for the game files.

On Linux build.sh ends with this step when flatpak-builder is installed;
--no-flatpak skips it. For distributing the build yourself only: it is not a
Flathub manifest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LFcBNQtF3Z7vfzi99BXwUe
---
 scripts/build-naot.sh | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scripts/build-naot.sh b/scripts/build-naot.sh
index 3fd12ae59..c3ab6fb85 100755
--- a/scripts/build-naot.sh
+++ b/scripts/build-naot.sh
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ detect_arch() {
 arch="${CUO_ARCH:-$(detect_arch)}"
 version=""
 dev_build=0
+flatpak=1
 
 while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do
   case "$1" in
@@ -36,6 +37,7 @@ while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do
     --out) output_directory="$2"; shift 2 ;;
     --version) version="$2"; shift 2 ;;
     --dev-build) dev_build=1; shift ;;
+    --no-flatpak) flatpak=0; shift ;;
     *) echo "unknown option: $1"; exit 1 ;;
   esac
 done
@@ -209,3 +211,12 @@ dotnet publish "$plugin_host_project" -c Release -o "$bin_directory" "${publish_
 strip_symbols
 write_launcher
 chmod_outputs
+
+# On Linux the build is also packed as a Flatpak bundle, when the tools are there.
+if [[ "$platform" == "Linux" && $flatpak -eq 1 ]]; then
+  if command -v flatpak-builder >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    bash "$script_dir/make-flatpak.sh" --dist "$output_directory"
+  else
+    echo "flatpak-builder not installed: no Flatpak bundle (--no-flatpak hides this)."
+  fi
+fi
